# tests/pins/tinycc.sha256 -- sha256 of what the TinyCC route builds that
# live-bootstrap does not publish.  Not part of tests/pins/outputs.sha256
# because only CHECK_TINYCC=1 builds the junction files.
#   tinycc/tcc-first   build-out/tinycc/tcc-first, the first tcc, compiled by
#                      seed Forth with Mes libc (tinycc/build-first-tcc.sh,
#                      856,568 bytes);
#                      the same in two checkouts at different paths
#   tinycc/tcc-first-i386
#                      build-out/tinycc/tcc-first-i386, the same program
#                      compiled by the i386 back end, cc/i386/
#                      (tinycc/build-first-tcc-i386.sh, 975,624 bytes);
#                      the same in two checkouts at different paths
#   tinycc/junction/usr/bin/tcc-boot0
#                      build-out/tinycc/junction-root/usr/bin/tcc-boot0, what
#                      the first tcc makes of tcc.c in live-bootstrap's
#                      pass1.kaem (tests/tinycc/junction-check.sh).  MesCC's
#                      tcc-mes makes ea464b2f...; from boot1 on the two
#                      routes have the same bytes.  It equals what the
#                      junction study's stand-ins built with gcc, tcc 0.9.27
#                      and seed-cc make (c1696e57...).
#   tinycc/bin-boot/*, tinycc/bin/*
#                      build-out/tinycc/bin-boot/ and bin/, the source
#                      preparation tools seed Forth builds in native mode
#                      against M2libc (tinycc/build-tools.sh);
#                      the same in two checkouts at different paths
#   tinycc/bin-i386/*  build-out/tinycc/bin-i386/, the same tools compiled
#                      by the i386 back end (tinycc/build-tools-i386.sh)
#   tinycc/hex0-handoff/boot1/...
#                      what boot 1 of tests/tinycc/hex0-handoff-check.sh
#                      hands to boot 2 besides tcc-mes and tcc-boot0: the
#                      mes libc tcc-mes makes (all but libc.a equal what
#                      live-bootstrap publishes after tcc-boot2) and the i386
#                      kaem, cp, chmod, match, rm and hex0-export the first
#                      tcc builds against it.  The old first tcc (7b2efd95,
#                      pnut's libc) gave the same bytes in the host
#                      junction (tinycc/lb-replay.sh stopped before
#                      "# Install") and under K0; the first tcc with Mes
#                      libc (d9e97270) gives them under K0.
# When a change is meant to alter one, update its line in the same commit
# and say why.
